       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen, and I know of no indication that supports it. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, or cardiovascular harm. It also wouldn't relieve pain any better, because ibuprofen's analgesic effect plateaus well below this dose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day).** This is the maximum labeled dose.\n- **Enter a lower dose,** such as 400 mg or 600 mg, at a frequency you choose.\n- **Add other pain control.** Scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen is a common way to get more analgesia without going over the NSAID ceiling.\n\nIf you think this dose is clinically justified, for example under a specific protocol, please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy. They can then enter or verify it through the proper override process. If you'd like one of the options above, tell me which and I'll enter it now."
